                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had this game for a long long time and I just kept dying to my wounds. I never hated it though. It was fairly realistic survival. Manage your resources, fight the wildlife, and carry on. I finally was able to finish the whole game just today because I had played enough of other games to be smart about rationing resources, not panic at enemies, and keep an eye on my stats.\n\nThis game is definitely for those survival lovers. I don't mind grindy games. The music is fantastic. I kept dying before but the reasons for dying were completely understandable to me. Resources are scarce but you kinda get the hang of where to find specific things. The dockable items show an icon and from the icon, you get an idea of what you find. Even when you dock it shows you exactly what to expect. \"Wilderness: limited supplies\" \"NJ Liquor: You'll find alcohol here\" \"Camp Site: Often has flint, always has a lit flame\" \"Church: Has rags, and stitching kits\" etc.\n\nThe rapids are a pain to navigate through especially on your base raft, but lets be real: You have a couple of planks trying to paddle through a flood. Of course it's hard. Once you get a rotor, you can turn super quick. For me, at least, navigating the boat was intuitive. If the rapids are too fast and you see a rock or debris coming up, you can pull back the left stick to slow down so you can dodge. You can manage how far you dodge my pulling your left stick immediately in the opposite direction after you paddle so you don't go as far and can weave through rocks without losing all your stamina. Don't bother trying to go against the current until you get a motor.\n\nIf you hate slow stories, they would hate this too. The main quest only has 3 points of progression separated by many regions which you have to stop on multiple islands for resources, so you stay in a region for about say 5-10 minutes. I personally don't mind it as I find this whole game cozy, and the music is absolutely fantastic.\n\nI would still recommend this though. Just understand that you will 10000000000% die multiple times as you learn what can kill you, manage your resources wrong, etc. I had to go through multiple islands running away from all the things because I ran out of flint and my stone knife broke which locked me out of the basic traps. It can happen. Always have extra of the basic materials. Never turn them all into something else. Craft as you need it.",
